## 3. PHASE 1 — DEEP RESEARCH FROM PRIMARY SOURCES

Perform real web research and verify the current state of every relevant source. Do not rely on remembered details or dates. Note access date, release/spec version/date when available, the relevant claim, Moonframe implication, confidence and whether the claim is directly stated or is your architectural inference.

### Priority official sources

Start with these and discover additional official sources as required:

1. **Design Tokens Community Group**
   - https://www.designtokens.org/
   - https://www.designtokens.org/tr/2025.10/
   - https://www.w3.org/community/reports/design-tokens/CG-FINAL-format-20251028/
   Verify which publication is current, whether it is a Community Group specification/report rather than a W3C Recommendation, which token types/aliases/metadata it supports, and which parts are mature enough for Moonframe. Do not claim full DTCG conformance if only a partial format is implemented.

2. **Tailwind CSS v4**
   - https://tailwindcss.com/docs/theme
   - https://tailwindcss.com/docs/dark-mode
   - https://tailwindcss.com/docs/colors
   - https://tailwindcss.com/docs/adding-custom-styles
   Verify the current syntax and behavior of `@theme`, CSS variables, utility generation, `@theme inline` if relevant, dark-mode variants, arbitrary values, scanning/source detection and runtime custom-property usage. Clearly separate build-time utility tokens from runtime theme values.

3. **shadcn/ui**
   - https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/theming
   - https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/installation
   - https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/changelog
   Review current theming conventions, CSS variable naming, default providers/styles and their current primitive-provider options. Treat this as a compatibility reference, not as Moonframe's canonical spec or an instruction to copy code.

4. **CSS standards and browser behavior**
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Using_CSS_custom_properties
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color-scheme
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/prefers-color-scheme
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/prefers-reduced-motion
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/forced-colors
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors
   - https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/
   - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@property
   Verify browser support and standard status before relying on advanced CSS behavior. Do not use an experimental feature as a required foundation without fallbacks.

5. **Accessibility**
   - https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/
   - https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/
   Research contrast, focus appearance, target size, non-text contrast, hover/focus states, text resizing, reflow, forced-colors and reduced-motion. Treat the relevant success criteria carefully; do not reduce accessibility to one contrast ratio.

6. **Token tooling and deterministic generation**
   - https://styledictionary.com/
   - https://github.com/style-dictionary/style-dictionary
   Research current Style Dictionary support for DTCG tokens, transforms, formats, custom transforms and version behavior. Compare with any genuinely suitable alternatives, but do not install a tool or select it without examining current maturity and outputs.

7. **React and framework/runtime behavior**
   - https://react.dev/
   - The official documentation for the framework actually found in this repository.
   Research context/state architecture, SSR/hydration implications, avoiding theme flash, script timing, client/server boundaries, and preference persistence. Do not assume Next.js if the repo does not use Next.js.

8. **Build validation and schema**
   Research official JSON Schema documentation and the selected validator's current compatibility/version. Prefer explicit schemas and deterministic validation for machine-readable contracts.

### Questions the research must answer

- What parts of DTCG are beneficial for Moonframe's source format, and what are the limits of the ecosystem/tooling today?
- Is the canonical token source better as DTCG JSON, a constrained DTCG-compatible JSON, or another typed source? Show evidence, trade-offs and a recommendation.
- Should Style Dictionary be used, or would a small deterministic generator be more maintainable? Evaluate expected transforms, CSS output, type output, source maps/debuggability and maintenance burden.
- What should Tailwind `@theme` generate, and what should remain runtime CSS custom properties?
- How should a root skin/mode attribute map to token values without creating unbounded dynamic class names?
- How can SSR avoid a flash of the wrong skin/mode while keeping user preference and resolved system mode distinct?
- What is a reliable contrast validation method across the proposed color formats, transparency, gradients, textured surfaces and states?
- Which runtime features must work in browsers with limited advanced color/CSS capabilities?
- What test coverage is possible without implementing the actual UI?

### Research log

Create or update `docs/research/token-theme-engine-research.md` or the equivalent existing canonical file. Each entry must include:

- research question;
- official source URL and publisher;
- publication/release/spec version/date if verified;
- access date;
- finding and exact relevant section;
- direct fact versus Moonframe interpretation;
- architecture consequence;
- alternative considered;
- confidence/remaining uncertainty.

Prefer primary sources and direct citations. Do not copy large passages from documentation. If two authoritative sources disagree, explain the distinction and record the decision rather than silently choosing one.

